{"step_index":2733,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T12:51:28Z","thinking":"Percentage formatting within the spreadsheet is now confirmed as working. The display is dynamic, correctly reflecting the underlying formula's calculations. Next, the focus shifts to how these review changes are applied within the desktop application.\n\n\nThe application loads the workbook, moves reviewed rows, and saves. This triggers formula recalculation in the spreadsheet, ensuring up-to-date counts. Subsequently, counts of matched, not found, and review rows are calculated.\n\nThe database is updated with these counts, and the application status is set to \"completed\" if no rows remain for review, otherwise \"reviewing.\" Finally, a statistics dictionary is returned reflecting the updated data.\n\n\nThe application's review application function retrieves updated statistics after processing. It displays a success message, including counts for matched, rejected, and remaining items. If new statistics are provided, those are loaded. The application also refreshes the history view. Error handling is implemented for both API failures and unexpected exceptions, providing informative messages to the user.\n\n\nThe UI issue appears to be caused by the loading modal's limited scope; it's likely hidden or inaccessible during re-run operations. The modal's structure must be changed to become a global overlay, resolving its availability issue. CSS adjustments are crucial to ensure the modal correctly covers the entire screen, blurring the background, and displaying correctly. Additionally, a global flag may be required to control the modal's display state.\n\n\nEnsuring only one process runs at a time requires coordinating UI and backend states. The UI will manage a global flag to prevent process initiation while a process is active, displaying a warning message via a toast notification. The backend requires a check to prevent process overlaps, ensuring a running thread isn't restarted.\n\n\nThe confidence display format is successfully enhanced, providing user-friendly output in the spreadsheet. Now, focusing on refining the matching logic to address brand versus generic scenarios in pharmaceutical data.\n\n\n\"بديل تجاري / مثيل: نفس المادة الفعالة والتركيز ولكن الاسم التجاري مختلف (المطلوب: رو اكيتان، المتوفر: ايزوتريتينوين)\"\n\"بديل تجاري / مثيل: نفس المادة الفعالة والتركيز ولكن الاسم التجاري مختلف (المطلوب: زوفيراكس، المتوفر: لوفير)\"\nإضافة قاعدة جديدة: إذا كان عدد العبوات مطابقًا (مثل ٣ أمبولات == ٣ امبولات)، أو مجرد تضمين الشركة المصنعة (مثل /نوفارتس)، فهي مطابقة تامة.\nبالنسبة لفصل بيئة الإنتاج عن بيئة التطوير، يتم تحديد المهام اللازمة للتأكد من أن النظام المختار منفصل عن بيئة التطوير.\n\n\nA script to package the production environment, building a clean distribution directory has been decided upon. The script will handle exclusions to create a minimal deployment package for the target machine. This package will include the core application code, requirements, configuration files, and a batch script for ease of setup. The batch script's functionality needs to include Python checking and requirement installation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan for Excel dynamic summary formulas, review toast & real-time sync, global re-run progress overlay, pharmaceutical prompt rules, and production deployment packaging.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Implementation Plan: Excel Dynamic Formulas, UI Synchronization, Clinical Rules & Production Packaging\n\nImplement dynamic Excel summary formulas, real-time UI synchronization for review actions, full-screen re-run overlay with concurrent process locking, clinical prompt refinement (brand vs generic / identical count), and a production deployment packager.\n\n## User Review Required\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> - **Excel Formulas in Summary Sheet**: The summary sheet will now use native Excel formulas (`=B3+B4+B5`, `=MAX(0, COUNTA(...) - 1)`, `=IF(...)`) so any edit in Excel or in the app updates all statistics dynamically.\n> - **Brand vs Generic Substitutions**: Drugs with the same active ingredient but different trade names (e.g., Roaccutane vs generic Isotretinoin, or Zovirax vs Lovir) will be routed to \"يحتاج مراجعة\" with an explicit Arabic reason instead of being automatically matched, giving pharmacists full control.\n> - **Concurrent Process Lock**: Once any matching process starts (new, restart, or re-run), the UI displays a full-screen backdrop with a live timer and blocks starting any new process until the current one finishes.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### 1. Output Engine (`src/output/excel_writer.py`)\n\n- **Dynamic Summary Sheet with Excel Formulas**:\n  - `إجمالي الأصناف المطلوبة`: `=B3+B4+B5`\n  - `تم مطابقتها`: `=SUM(B8:B{7+N})` (sums warehouse matches)\n  - `لم يُعثر عليها`: `=MAX(0, COUNTA('لم يُعثر عليه'!A:A)-1)`\n  - `تحتاج مراجعة`: `=MAX(0, COUNTA('يحتاج مراجعة'!A:A)-1)`\n  - Warehouse details table (rows 8+):\n    - Col 2: `=MAX(0, COUNTA('{warehouse_sheet}'!A:A)-1)`\n    - Col 3: `=COUNTIF('يحتاج مراجعة'!D:D, \"{warehouse_name}\")`\n  - Percentages formatted dynamically with `=IF(B2>0, B3/B2, 0)` and format `0.0%`.\n- **Friendly Match Confidence in Arabic**:\n  - Format raw values (`exact`, `high (0.95)`, `llm`) into professional Arabic:\n    - `exact` -> `تطابق تام (100%)`\n    - `high (X.XX)` -> `تطابق نصي دقيق (X%)`\n    - `llm` -> `مطابقة ذكية (AI)`\n    - `تأكيد يدوي (مراجعة)` -> `تأكيد يدوي (مراجعة)`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Desktop App Backend (`desktop_app/backend.py`)\n\n- **Concurrency Protection**:\n  - Check if `self._worker_thread and self._worker_thread.is_alive()` in `start_process`, `restart_process`, and `rerun_process`.\n  - Return `{\"success\": False, \"error\": \"توجد عملية مطابقة قيد التشغيل حالياً، يرجى الانتظار حتى تنتهي\"}`.\n- **Enhanced `apply_reviews`**:\n  - Recalculate and update the `ملخص` sheet cells in openpyxl when decisions are applied.\n  - Compute `new_stats`: `matched_count`, `not_found_count`, `review_count`, `total`.\n  - Update `data/history.db` process record with updated counts and status (`completed` if 0 remaining, else `reviewing`).\n  - Return `new_stats` in the JSON response for instant UI update.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Frontend UI (`desktop_app/templates/index.html`)\n\n- **Global Progress Overlay**:\n  - Move `#progress-modal` outside `#screen-new` to make it a global fixed overlay (`position: fixed; width: 100vw; height: 100vh; z-index: 99999`).\n  - When re-running or starting a process, the overlay appears over the entire window with a spinner, live timer, and progress message.\n- **Process State & Buttons Lock**:\n  - Add `window.isProcessRunning = false`.\n  - Disable / prevent submit if a process is running.\n- **Fix Review Toast & Instant Screen Update**:\n  - Update `applyReviews()` to display friendly Arabic message:\n    `تم اعتماد: X صنف مطابق، Y غير متوفر، والمتبقي للمراجعة: Z` (removes `undefined`).\n  - Call `loadResults(result.new_stats)` so the stat cards update on screen immediately without navigating to History and back.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Matching Engine & System Prompt (`src/fast_match/coordinator.py`)\n\n- **Brand vs Generic / Different Brand Rule**:\n  - Same active ingredient but different brand name (e.g. Roaccutane vs Isotretinoin, Zovirax vs Lovir) -> return `\"status\": \"review\"` with reason `\"بديل تجاري / مثيل: نفس المادة الفعالة والتركيز ولكن الاسم التجاري مختلف\"`.\n- **Identical Count / Manufacturer Rule**:\n  - If counts are identical (e.g. 3 ampoules == ٣ امبولات) or only manufacturer differs (/نوفارتس, /اكاديميا) -> return `\"status\": \"match\"`, NEVER mark as review.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Production Packager & Setup Scripts\n\n- **`scripts/package_production.py`**:\n  - Copies all necessary runtime code (`desktop_app`, `src`, `fast_main.py`, `requirements.txt`, `.env.example`).\n  - Excludes dev artifacts, git files, temporary databases, test files, and caches.\n  - Prepares a fresh `data/` directory with clean SQLite schema.\n- **`run_app.bat`**:\n  - Windows batch launcher that activates virtual environment or installs requirements, sets configuration, and starts the desktop app with one click.\n- **`README_SETUP.md`**:\n  - Clear Arabic instructions for installing and running on the target PC.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n### Automated / Python Verification\n1. Run `python -c \"...\"` to verify Excel summary formula generation and `openpyxl` formula evaluation.\n2. Run a mock `apply_reviews` test on `PROC-003` to verify:\n   - Excel `ملخص` sheet updates.\n   - Database record updates.\n   - Response includes `new_stats`.\n3. Verify `FastCoordinator` prompt changes against test cases (Roaccutane vs Isotretinoin -> review; Voltaren 3 ampoules vs Voltaren 3 ampoules/Novartis -> match).\n4. Run `package_production.py` and verify created directory structure and file contents.\n\n### Manual Verification\n- Test `applyReviews()` in the webview interface.\n- Test \"إعادة المطابقة (Re-run)\" button and verify global modal appears with live timer.\n","Description":"Implementation plan for Excel dynamic formulas, review sync, modal overlay, prompt tuning, and production packager","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Writing implementation plan","toolSummary":"Create implementation_plan.md"}}]}
